/-!
# Global tessellations from local tessellations

Let a group `G` act by isometries on a simply connected, locally connected metric space `X`, and
let `P ⊆ X` be a closed path-connected tile. A *local tiling* assigns to each point `x ∈ P` a
set `N x ⊆ G` of *local neighbours*: the elements `h` for which `h • P` is meant to be
one of the tiles around `x`. The sets `N x` are required to behave like the tiles around a point
of an actual tessellation:

* `1 ∈ N x`, and `x ∈ h • P` for `h ∈ N x`;
* the neighbours of `x`, seen from the tile `h • P`, are `h⁻¹ • N x`: if `h ∈ N x` then
  `h⁻¹ ∈ N (h⁻¹ • x)`, and `h * k ∈ N x` for `k ∈ N (h⁻¹ • x)`;
* every point of `P` lies in a *tiling chart* built from its own neighbours.

A tiling chart `(W, M)` is an open set `W` covered, locally finitely, by tiles `h • P` with
`h ∈ M`, such that at every point of `W` the tiles of `M` through it are exactly the translates
of the local neighbours there. Charts need not come from a single point: near an ideal vertex of
a hyperbolic polygon the natural chart has infinitely many tiles.

The main theorem says that local tilings with charts of uniform size are restrictions of one
global tessellation. Let `Γ` be the subgroup generated by all local neighbours. Then the
translates `γ • P`, `γ ∈ Γ`, cover `X` and are locally finite, and the only coincidences between
them are the local ones: if `γ ∈ Γ` carries a point `x ∈ P` to a point of `P`, then `γ` is a
local neighbour at `γ • x`. The uniformity hypothesis holds automatically when `P` is compact.

This is the covering-space core of Poincaré's polygon theorem. There the tile is a side-paired
hyperbolic polygon, the local neighbours at a point are the tiles met by following the side
pairings around it, and the angle and cycle conditions at the vertices are what make them a
local tiling; the conclusion then says that the polygon is a fundamental domain for the group
generated by the side pairings.

The proof glues copies `{a} × P`, `a ∈ G`, identifying `(a, x)` with `(b, y)` when
`a • x = b • y` and `a⁻¹ * b ∈ N x`. The map `(a, x) ↦ a • x` from the glued space to `X` has a
continuous local section through every point, read off from a chart, over a ball of uniform
radius, and the glued space is Hausdorff because every point has a chart of its own; so this map
is a covering map. The copies indexed by `Γ` are joined by paths, since `P` is path-connected
and the copies indexed by `a` and `a * h` meet for each local neighbour `h`. As `X` is simply
connected, the covering map is injective on them.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.IsTilingChart P N W M`: `W` is an open set tiled by the translates `h • P`, `h ∈ M`,
  compatibly with the local neighbours `N`.
* `TauCeti.IsLocalTiling P N`: the sets `N x` are local neighbours of a local tiling by `P`.
* `TauCeti.HasUniformTilingCharts P N`: tiling charts of a uniform size are available at every
  point of `P`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.IsLocalTiling.hasUniformTilingCharts_of_isCompact`: a compact tile has uniform tiling
  charts.
* `TauCeti.IsLocalTiling.mem_of_smul_mem`: an element of `Γ` carrying a point of `P` into `P` is
  a local neighbour at the image point.
* `TauCeti.IsLocalTiling.iUnion_smul_eq_univ`: uniform tiling charts imply that the translates
  of `P` by `Γ` cover a preconnected pseudometric space `X`.
* `TauCeti.IsLocalTiling.locallyFinite_smul`: the translates of `P` by `Γ` are locally finite.

## References

* Bernard Maskit, *On Poincaré's theorem for fundamental polygons*, Adv. Math. 7 (1971),
  219–230.
* David B. A. Epstein and Carlo Petronio, *An exposition of Poincaré's polyhedron theorem*,
  Enseign. Math. (2) 40 (1994), 113–170.
* Alan Beardon, *The Geometry of Discrete Groups*, Graduate Texts in Mathematics 91, Springer,
  1983, Chapter 9.
-/

public section

open Set Metric Topology
open scoped Pointwise

namespace TauCeti

variable {G X : Type*} [Group G] [MulAction G X]

section Defs

variable [TopologicalSpace X]

/-- A **tiling chart** for the local neighbours `N` of a tile `P`: an open set `W` covered,
locally finitely, by the tiles `h • P` with `h ∈ M`, such that at each point of `W` the tiles of
`M` through that point are exactly the translates of the local neighbours there. Precisely, if
`h ∈ M` and `v ∈ P` with `h • v ∈ W`, then `h • N v ⊆ M`, and every `h' ∈ M` with
`h • v ∈ h' • P` lies in `h • N v`. -/
structure IsTilingChart (P : Set X) (N : X → Set G) (W : Set X) (M : Set G) : Prop where
  /-- The domain of the chart is open. -/
  isOpen : IsOpen W
  /-- The tiles of the chart cover its domain. -/
  subset_iUnion_smul : W ⊆ ⋃ h ∈ M, h • P
  /-- The tiles of the chart, cut down to its domain, are locally finite. -/
  locallyFinite : LocallyFinite fun h : M ↦ (h : G) • P ∩ W
  /-- The translated local neighbours at a point of the domain are tiles of the chart. -/
  mul_mem : ∀ h ∈ M, ∀ v ∈ P, h • v ∈ W → ∀ k ∈ N v, h * k ∈ M
  /-- Every tile of the chart through a point of the domain is a translated local neighbour. -/
  inv_mul_mem : ∀ h ∈ M, ∀ v ∈ P, h • v ∈ W → ∀ h' ∈ M, h • v ∈ h' • P → h⁻¹ * h' ∈ N v

/-- A **local tiling** by a closed path-connected tile `P`: for each `x ∈ P`, `N x` is a set of
local neighbours, the elements `h` such that `h • P` is one of the tiles around `x`. The
identity is a neighbour, `x ∈ h • P` for each neighbour `h`, the neighbours of `x` seen from the
tile `h • P` are the translates `h⁻¹ • N x`, and each point of `P` lies in a tiling chart made of
its own neighbours. -/
structure IsLocalTiling (P : Set X) (N : X → Set G) : Prop where
  /-- The tile is closed. -/
  isClosed : IsClosed P
  /-- The tile is path-connected. -/
  isPathConnected : IsPathConnected P
  /-- The tile itself is a neighbour of each of its points. -/
  one_mem : ∀ x ∈ P, (1 : G) ∈ N x
  /-- Each point lies in its neighbouring tiles. -/
  inv_smul_mem : ∀ x ∈ P, ∀ h ∈ N x, h⁻¹ • x ∈ P
  /-- Seen from a neighbouring tile, the tile `P` is again a neighbour. -/
  inv_mem : ∀ x ∈ P, ∀ h ∈ N x, h⁻¹ ∈ N (h⁻¹ • x)
  /-- Neighbours of a neighbouring tile are neighbours. -/
  mul_mem : ∀ x ∈ P, ∀ h ∈ N x, ∀ k ∈ N (h⁻¹ • x), h * k ∈ N x
  /-- Each point lies in a tiling chart made of its own neighbours. -/
  exists_isTilingChart : ∀ x ∈ P, ∃ W, x ∈ W ∧ IsTilingChart P N W (N x)

end Defs

section Uniform

variable [PseudoMetricSpace X] {P : Set X} {N : X → Set G}

variable (P N) in
/-- A local tiling has **uniform tiling charts** if there is a radius `ε > 0` such that for each
point `y ∈ P` some tiling chart `(W, M)`, with `M` in the group generated by the local
neighbours, contains the ball of radius `ε` about a translate `h • y` with `h ∈ M`. -/
def HasUniformTilingCharts : Prop :=
  ∃ ε > 0, ∀ y ∈ P, ∃ W M, IsTilingChart P N W M ∧ M ⊆ Subgroup.closure (⋃ x ∈ P, N x) ∧
    ∃ h ∈ M, ball (h • y) ε ⊆ W

theorem hasUniformTilingCharts_iff : HasUniformTilingCharts P N ↔
    ∃ ε > 0, ∀ y ∈ P, ∃ W M, IsTilingChart P N W M ∧ M ⊆ Subgroup.closure (⋃ x ∈ P, N x) ∧
      ∃ h ∈ M, ball (h • y) ε ⊆ W :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- **A compact tile has uniform tiling charts.** -/
theorem IsLocalTiling.hasUniformTilingCharts_of_isCompact (hP : IsLocalTiling P N)
    (hc : IsCompact P) : HasUniformTilingCharts P N := by
  -- a Lebesgue number for the charts of the points of `P` is a uniform radius
  choose! W hxW hW using hP.exists_isTilingChart
  obtain ⟨δ, hδ, hball⟩ := lebesgue_number_lemma_of_metric hc (c := fun x : P ↦ W x)
    (fun x ↦ (hW x x.2).isOpen) fun x hx ↦ mem_iUnion.2 ⟨⟨x, hx⟩, hxW x hx⟩
  refine ⟨δ, hδ, fun y hy ↦ ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨⟨c, hc⟩, hyc⟩ := hball y hy
  exact ⟨W c, N c, hW c hc, fun _ hk ↦ Subgroup.subset_closure (mem_iUnion₂.2 ⟨c, hc, hk⟩),
    1, hP.one_mem c hc, by rwa [one_smul]⟩

/-- **The translates of the tile cover the space.** For a local tiling with uniform charts of a
preconnected pseudometric space acted on by isometries, the translates of `P` by the group
generated by the local neighbours cover the space. -/
theorem IsLocalTiling.iUnion_smul_eq_univ [IsIsometricSMul G X] [PreconnectedSpace X]
    (hP : IsLocalTiling P N) (hu : HasUniformTilingCharts P N) :
    ⋃ γ ∈ Subgroup.closure (⋃ x ∈ P, N x), γ • P = univ := by
  -- the union is open by the charts of the points of `P`, and closed because a uniform chart
  -- around a nearby point of the union reaches every point within the uniform radius
  set Γ := Subgroup.closure (⋃ x ∈ P, N x)
  obtain ⟨ε, hε, hunif⟩ := hu
  obtain ⟨y₀, hy₀⟩ := hP.isPathConnected.nonempty
  refine IsClopen.eq_univ ⟨isClosed_of_closure_subset fun z hz ↦ ?_,
    isOpen_iff_forall_mem_open.2 fun z hz ↦ ?_⟩
    ⟨y₀, mem_iUnion₂.2 ⟨1, Γ.one_mem, by rwa [one_smul]⟩⟩
  · -- a point near `z` lies on a tile, and a uniform chart there reaches `z`
    obtain ⟨w, hw, hzw⟩ := Metric.mem_closure_iff.1 hz ε hε
    obtain ⟨γ, hγ, hwγ⟩ := mem_iUnion₂.1 hw
    obtain ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩ := mem_smul_set.1 hwγ
    obtain ⟨W, M, hc, hMΓ, h, hh, hball⟩ := hunif y hy
    have hzW : (h * γ⁻¹) • z ∈ W := hball <| by
      have hy' : h • y = (h * γ⁻¹) • γ • y := by rw [mul_smul, inv_smul_smul]
      rw [mem_ball, hy', dist_smul]
      exact hzw
    obtain ⟨h', hh', hzh'⟩ := mem_iUnion₂.1 (hc.subset_iUnion_smul hzW)
    refine mem_iUnion₂.2 ⟨γ * h⁻¹ * h', Γ.mul_mem (Γ.mul_mem hγ (Γ.inv_mem (hMΓ hh))) (hMΓ hh'),
      ?_⟩
    rw [mem_smul_set_iff_inv_smul_mem, mul_inv_rev, mul_inv_rev, inv_inv, mul_smul, mul_smul]
    rwa [mem_smul_set_iff_inv_smul_mem, mul_smul] at hzh'
  · -- the chart of a point of `P` translates to a neighbourhood covered by tiles
    obtain ⟨γ, hγ, hzγ⟩ := mem_iUnion₂.1 hz
    obtain ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩ := mem_smul_set.1 hzγ
    obtain ⟨W, hyW, hc⟩ := hP.exists_isTilingChart y hy
    refine ⟨γ • W, fun w hw ↦ ?_, hc.isOpen.smul γ, smul_mem_smul_set hyW⟩
    obtain ⟨u, hu, rfl⟩ := mem_smul_set.1 hw
    obtain ⟨h, hh, huh⟩ := mem_iUnion₂.1 (hc.subset_iUnion_smul hu)
    refine mem_iUnion₂.2
      ⟨γ * h, Γ.mul_mem hγ (Subgroup.subset_closure (mem_iUnion₂.2 ⟨y, hy, hh⟩)), ?_⟩
    rw [mul_smul]
    exact smul_mem_smul_set huh

end Uniform

variable [MetricSpace X] {P : Set X} {N : X → Set G}

/-! ### The space glued from copies of the tile -/

section Gluing

/-- The gluing relation on `Σ a, P`, identifying `(a, x)` with `(b, y)` when `a • x = b • y` and
`a⁻¹ * b` is a local neighbour at `x`. -/
private def tilingSetoid (hP : IsLocalTiling P N) : Setoid (Σ _ : G, P) where
  r y z := y.1 • (y.2 : X) = z.1 • (z.2 : X) ∧ y.1⁻¹ * z.1 ∈ N y.2
  iseqv :=
    { refl y := ⟨rfl, by simpa using hP.one_mem _ y.2.2⟩
      symm := by
        rintro ⟨a, x⟩ ⟨b, y⟩ ⟨hxy, hab⟩
        refine ⟨hxy.symm, ?_⟩
        have hy : (a⁻¹ * b)⁻¹ • (x : X) = y := by
          rw [mul_inv_rev, inv_inv, mul_smul, hxy, inv_smul_smul]
        have h := hP.inv_mem _ x.2 _ hab
        dsimp only at h ⊢
        rw [hy, mul_inv_rev, inv_inv] at h
        exact h
      trans := by
        rintro ⟨a, x⟩ ⟨b, y⟩ ⟨c, z⟩ ⟨hxy, hab⟩ ⟨hyz, hbc⟩
        refine ⟨hxy.trans hyz, ?_⟩
        have hy : (a⁻¹ * b)⁻¹ • (x : X) = y := by
          rw [mul_inv_rev, inv_inv, mul_smul, hxy, inv_smul_smul]
        have := hP.mul_mem _ x.2 _ hab (b⁻¹ * c) (by rwa [hy])
        rwa [mul_assoc, mul_inv_cancel_left] at this }

/-- The space glued from the copies `{a} × P` of the tile. -/
private abbrev Glued (hP : IsLocalTiling P N) : Type _ :=
  Quotient (tilingSetoid hP)

/-- The point `x` of the copy of the tile indexed by `a`. -/
private def glue (hP : IsLocalTiling P N) (a : G) (x : P) : Glued hP :=
  Quotient.mk _ ⟨a, x⟩

private theorem exists_glue_eq (hP : IsLocalTiling P N) (e : Glued hP) :
    ∃ a x, glue hP a x = e := by
  obtain ⟨⟨a, x⟩, rfl⟩ := Quotient.exists_rep e
  exact ⟨a, x, rfl⟩

private theorem glue_eq_glue_iff (hP : IsLocalTiling P N) {a b : G} {x y : P} :
    glue hP a x = glue hP b y ↔ a • (x : X) = b • (y : X) ∧ a⁻¹ * b ∈ N x :=
  Quotient.eq

/-- The projection of the glued space to `X`, sending `(a, x)` to `a • x`. -/
private def proj (hP : IsLocalTiling P N) : Glued hP → X :=
  Quotient.lift (fun y ↦ y.1 • (y.2 : X)) fun _ _ h ↦ h.1

private theorem proj_glue (hP : IsLocalTiling P N) (a : G) (x : P) :
    proj hP (glue hP a x) = a • (x : X) :=
  rfl

private theorem continuous_glue (hP : IsLocalTiling P N) (a : G) : Continuous (glue hP a) :=
  continuous_quotient_mk'.comp continuous_sigmaMk

/-- Left translation of the glued space by `g`, sending `(a, x)` to `(g * a, x)`. -/
private def translate (hP : IsLocalTiling P N) (g : G) : Glued hP → Glued hP :=
  Quotient.lift (fun y ↦ glue hP (g * y.1) y.2) fun _ _ h ↦ (glue_eq_glue_iff hP).2
    ⟨by simp only [mul_smul, h.1], by simpa only [mul_inv_rev, mul_assoc, inv_mul_cancel_left]
      using h.2⟩

private theorem translate_glue (hP : IsLocalTiling P N) (g a : G) (x : P) :
    translate hP g (glue hP a x) = glue hP (g * a) x :=
  rfl

private theorem continuous_translate (hP : IsLocalTiling P N) (g : G) :
    Continuous (translate hP g) :=
  Continuous.quotient_lift (continuous_sigma fun a ↦ continuous_glue hP (g * a)) _

/-- In the glued space, the point `(1, x)` is joined by a path to every point of a copy indexed
by the group generated by the local neighbours. -/
private theorem joined_glue (hP : IsLocalTiling P N) {γ : G}
    (hγ : γ ∈ Subgroup.closure (⋃ x ∈ P, N x)) (x y : P) :
    Joined (glue hP 1 x) (glue hP γ y) := by
  have hsheet (a : G) (x y : P) : Joined (glue hP a x) (glue hP a y) :=
    ((hP.isPathConnected.joinedIn x x.2 y y.2).joined_subtype).map (continuous_glue hP a)
  induction hγ using Subgroup.closure_induction generalizing x y with
  | mem g hg =>
    obtain ⟨x₀, hx₀, hg⟩ := mem_iUnion₂.1 hg
    have heq : glue hP 1 ⟨x₀, hx₀⟩ = glue hP g ⟨g⁻¹ • x₀, hP.inv_smul_mem x₀ hx₀ g hg⟩ :=
      (glue_eq_glue_iff hP).2 ⟨by simp, by simpa using hg⟩
    exact (hsheet 1 x _).trans (by rw [heq]; exact hsheet g _ y)
  | one => exact hsheet 1 x y
  | mul a b _ _ iha ihb =>
    have := (ihb x y).map (continuous_translate hP a)
    rw [translate_glue, translate_glue, mul_one] at this
    exact (iha x x).trans this
  | inv a _ ih =>
    have := (ih y x).map (continuous_translate hP a⁻¹)
    rw [translate_glue, translate_glue, mul_one, inv_mul_cancel] at this
    exact this.symm

/-! ### Local sections from tiling charts -/

open scoped Classical in
/-- The lift of a point `u` of a chart `(W, M)` to the glued space, in the copy of the chart
translated by `g`: if `u ∈ h • P` with `h ∈ M`, this is the point `h⁻¹ • u` of the copy indexed
by `g * h`. The default `e₀` is used only off the tiles of the chart. -/
private noncomputable def chartLift (hP : IsLocalTiling P N) (M : Set G) (g : G) (e₀ : Glued hP)
    (u : X) : Glued hP :=
  if hu : ∃ h ∈ M, u ∈ h • P then
    glue hP (g * hu.choose) ⟨hu.choose⁻¹ • u, mem_smul_set_iff_inv_smul_mem.1 hu.choose_spec.2⟩
  else e₀

variable {W : Set X} {M : Set G}

/-- On a chart, the lift does not depend on the tile through the point. -/
private theorem chartLift_eq (hP : IsLocalTiling P N) (hc : IsTilingChart P N W M) (g : G)
    (e₀ : Glued hP) {u : X} (hu : u ∈ W) {h : G} (hh : h ∈ M) (huh : u ∈ h • P) :
    chartLift hP M g e₀ u = glue hP (g * h) ⟨h⁻¹ • u, mem_smul_set_iff_inv_smul_mem.1 huh⟩ := by
  have hex : ∃ h ∈ M, u ∈ h • P := ⟨h, hh, huh⟩
  rw [chartLift, dite_eq_left hex, glue_eq_glue_iff]
  obtain ⟨hh₀, hu₀⟩ := hex.choose_spec
  refine ⟨by simp only [mul_smul, smul_inv_smul], ?_⟩
  rw [mul_inv_rev, mul_assoc, inv_mul_cancel_left]
  exact hc.inv_mul_mem _ hh₀ _ (mem_smul_set_iff_inv_smul_mem.1 hu₀) (by rwa [smul_inv_smul]) h hh
    (by rwa [smul_inv_smul])

private theorem chartLift_smul (hP : IsLocalTiling P N) (hc : IsTilingChart P N W M) (g : G)
    (e₀ : Glued hP) {h : G} (hh : h ∈ M) {v : X} (hv : v ∈ P) (hvW : h • v ∈ W) :
    chartLift hP M g e₀ (h • v) = glue hP (g * h) ⟨v, hv⟩ := by
  rw [chartLift_eq hP hc g e₀ hvW hh (smul_mem_smul_set hv)]
  simp only [inv_smul_smul]

private theorem proj_chartLift (hP : IsLocalTiling P N) (hc : IsTilingChart P N W M) (g : G)
    (e₀ : Glued hP) {u : X} (hu : u ∈ W) : proj hP (chartLift hP M g e₀ u) = g • u := by
  obtain ⟨h, hh, huh⟩ := mem_iUnion₂.1 (hc.subset_iUnion_smul hu)
  rw [chartLift_eq hP hc g e₀ hu hh huh, proj_glue, mul_smul, smul_inv_smul]

variable [IsIsometricSMul G X]

private theorem continuous_proj (hP : IsLocalTiling P N) : Continuous (proj hP) :=
  Continuous.quotient_lift
    (continuous_sigma fun a ↦ (continuous_const_smul a).comp continuous_subtype_val) _

/-- The lift from a chart is continuous on the chart: near each point it is pieced together
from finitely many tiles, on each of which it is a translate of the inclusion of the tile. -/
private theorem continuousOn_chartLift (hP : IsLocalTiling P N) (hc : IsTilingChart P N W M)
    (g : G) (e₀ : Glued hP) : ContinuousOn (chartLift hP M g e₀) W := by
  intro u₀ hu₀
  obtain ⟨t, ht, hfin⟩ := hc.locallyFinite u₀
  obtain ⟨r, hr, hrt⟩ := Metric.mem_nhds_iff.1 (Filter.inter_mem (hc.isOpen.mem_nhds hu₀) ht)
  set K := closedBall u₀ (r / 2)
  have hKW : K ⊆ W ∩ t := (closedBall_subset_ball (half_lt_self hr)).trans hrt
  set F := {h : M | ((h : G) • P ∩ W ∩ t).Nonempty}
  have : Finite F := hfin.to_subtype
  have hcont : ContinuousOn (chartLift hP M g e₀) (⋃ h : F, ((h : G) • P ∩ K)) := by
    refine (locallyFinite_of_finite _).continuousOn_iUnion
      (fun h ↦ (hP.isClosed.smul _).inter isClosed_closedBall) fun h ↦ ?_
    refine ContinuousOn.mono (s := (h : G) • P ∩ W) ?_ (inter_subset_inter_right _
      (hKW.trans inter_subset_left))
    rw [continuousOn_iff_continuous_domRestrict]
    have heq : ((h : G) • P ∩ W).domRestrict (chartLift hP M g e₀) =
        fun u : ↥((h : G) • P ∩ W) ↦
          glue hP (g * h) ⟨(h : G)⁻¹ • (u : X), mem_smul_set_iff_inv_smul_mem.1 u.2.1⟩ :=
      funext fun u ↦ chartLift_eq hP hc g e₀ u.2.2 h.1.2 u.2.1
    rw [heq]
    exact (continuous_glue hP _).comp
      (((continuous_const_smul _).comp continuous_subtype_val).subtype_mk _)
  have hK : K ⊆ ⋃ h : F, ((h : G) • P ∩ K) := fun u hu ↦ by
    obtain ⟨h, hh, huh⟩ := mem_iUnion₂.1 (hc.subset_iUnion_smul (hKW hu).1)
    exact mem_iUnion.2 ⟨⟨⟨h, hh⟩, u, ⟨huh, (hKW hu).1⟩, (hKW hu).2⟩, huh, hu⟩
  exact ((hcont.mono hK).continuousAt (closedBall_mem_nhds _ (half_pos hr))).continuousWithinAt

/-- The lift from a chart maps open subsets of the chart to open sets: a point `(a, x)` of the
image stays in the image when `x` moves within `P`, since `g⁻¹ * a` is then a tile of the
chart. -/
private theorem isOpen_image_chartLift (hP : IsLocalTiling P N) (hc : IsTilingChart P N W M)
    (g : G) (e₀ : Glued hP) {B : Set X} (hB : IsOpen B) (hBW : B ⊆ W) :
    IsOpen (chartLift hP M g e₀ '' B) := by
  rw [← isQuotientMap_quotient_mk'.isOpen_preimage, isOpen_sigma_iff]
  intro a
  refine isOpen_iff_forall_mem_open.2 fun x hx ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨u, hu, hux⟩ := hx
  obtain ⟨h, hh, huh⟩ := mem_iUnion₂.1 (hc.subset_iUnion_smul (hBW hu))
  rw [chartLift_eq hP hc g e₀ (hBW hu) hh huh] at hux
  obtain ⟨hgu, hk⟩ := (glue_eq_glue_iff hP).1 hux
  have hga : g⁻¹ * a ∈ M := by
    have := hc.mul_mem h hh _ (mem_smul_set_iff_inv_smul_mem.1 huh)
      (by rw [smul_inv_smul]; exact hBW hu) _ hk
    rwa [mul_inv_rev, ← mul_assoc, mul_inv_cancel_left] at this
  refine ⟨{x' | g⁻¹ • a • (x' : X) ∈ B}, fun x' hx' ↦ ⟨_, hx', ?_⟩,
    hB.preimage ((continuous_const_smul _).comp ((continuous_const_smul _).comp
      continuous_subtype_val)), ?_⟩
  · rw [← mul_smul, chartLift_smul hP hc g e₀ hga x'.2 (by rw [mul_smul]; exact hBW hx'),
      mul_inv_cancel_left]
    -- `glue hP a x'` is by definition the class of `⟨a, x'⟩`
    rfl
  · rw [mem_ofPred_eq, ← hgu, mul_smul, smul_inv_smul, inv_smul_smul]
    exact hu

/-- The glued space is Hausdorff. Points with distinct projections are separated by the
projection. Two points `(a₁, x₁)` and `(a₂, x₂)` over the same point are separated by the lifts of
the charts of `x₁` and `x₂`: a common point of the two lifts would make `a₁⁻¹ * a₂` a local
neighbour at `x₁`. -/
private theorem t2Space_glued (hP : IsLocalTiling P N) : T2Space (Glued hP) := by
  refine ⟨fun e₁ e₂ hne ↦ ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨a₁, x₁, rfl⟩ := exists_glue_eq hP e₁
  obtain ⟨a₂, x₂, rfl⟩ := exists_glue_eq hP e₂
  by_cases hz : proj hP (glue hP a₁ x₁) ≠ proj hP (glue hP a₂ x₂)
  · obtain ⟨u, v, hu, hv, hzu, hzv, huv⟩ := t2_separation hz
    exact ⟨_, _, hu.preimage (continuous_proj hP), hv.preimage (continuous_proj hP), hzu, hzv,
      huv.preimage _⟩
  rw [not_not, proj_glue, proj_glue] at hz
  obtain ⟨W₁, hx₁, hc₁⟩ := hP.exists_isTilingChart x₁ x₁.2
  obtain ⟨W₂, hx₂, hc₂⟩ := hP.exists_isTilingChart x₂ x₂.2
  set e₁ := glue hP a₁ x₁
  set e₂ := glue hP a₂ x₂
  have hmem (a : G) (x : P) (W : Set X) (hx : (x : X) ∈ W) (hc : IsTilingChart P N W (N x)) :
      glue hP a x ∈ chartLift hP (N x) a (glue hP a x) '' W := by
    refine ⟨x, hx, ?_⟩
    have := chartLift_smul hP hc a (glue hP a x) (hP.one_mem x x.2) x.2 (by rwa [one_smul])
    rwa [one_smul, mul_one] at this
  refine ⟨_, _, isOpen_image_chartLift hP hc₁ a₁ e₁ hc₁.isOpen subset_rfl,
    isOpen_image_chartLift hP hc₂ a₂ e₂ hc₂.isOpen subset_rfl, hmem a₁ x₁ W₁ hx₁ hc₁,
    hmem a₂ x₂ W₂ hx₂ hc₂, disjoint_left.2 ?_⟩
  rintro _ ⟨u₁, hu₁, rfl⟩ ⟨u₂, hu₂, he⟩
  obtain ⟨h₁, hh₁, hu₁h⟩ := mem_iUnion₂.1 (hc₁.subset_iUnion_smul hu₁)
  obtain ⟨h₂, hh₂, hu₂h⟩ := mem_iUnion₂.1 (hc₂.subset_iUnion_smul hu₂)
  rw [chartLift_eq hP hc₁ a₁ e₁ hu₁ hh₁ hu₁h, chartLift_eq hP hc₂ a₂ e₂ hu₂ hh₂ hu₂h] at he
  obtain ⟨-, hk⟩ := (glue_eq_glue_iff hP).1 he.symm
  -- `a₁⁻¹ * a₂ * h₂` is a neighbour at `x₁`, hence so is `a₁⁻¹ * a₂`
  have h₁₂ : a₁⁻¹ * a₂ * h₂ ∈ N x₁ := by
    have := hc₁.mul_mem h₁ hh₁ _ (mem_smul_set_iff_inv_smul_mem.1 hu₁h)
      (by rwa [smul_inv_smul]) _ hk
    rwa [mul_inv_rev, ← mul_assoc, mul_inv_cancel_left, ← mul_assoc] at this
  have hx : (a₁⁻¹ * a₂ * h₂)⁻¹ • (x₁ : X) = h₂⁻¹ • (x₂ : X) := by
    rw [mul_inv_rev, mul_smul, mul_inv_rev, inv_inv, mul_smul, hz, inv_smul_smul]
  have := hP.mul_mem _ x₁.2 _ h₁₂ h₂⁻¹ (by rw [hx]; exact hP.inv_mem _ x₂.2 _ hh₂)
  rw [mul_inv_cancel_right] at this
  exact hne ((glue_eq_glue_iff hP).2 ⟨hz, this⟩)

variable [LocallyConnectedSpace X]

/-- **The glued space covers `X`.** Through each point `(a, y)` the lift of a uniform chart for
`y` gives a section of the projection over the ball of the uniform radius about `a • y`. -/
private theorem isCoveringMap_proj (hP : IsLocalTiling P N)
    (hu : HasUniformTilingCharts P N) : IsCoveringMap (proj hP) := by
  have := t2Space_glued hP
  obtain ⟨ε, hε, hunif⟩ := hu
  refine .of_forall_exists_section (continuous_proj hP) hε fun e ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨a, y, rfl⟩ := exists_glue_eq hP e
  obtain ⟨W, M, hc, -, h, hh, hball⟩ := hunif y y.2
  set g := a * h⁻¹
  have hgy : g⁻¹ • a • (y : X) = h • (y : X) := by
    rw [← mul_smul, mul_inv_rev, inv_inv, mul_assoc, inv_mul_cancel, mul_one]
  have hmaps : g⁻¹ • ball (proj hP (glue hP a y)) ε = ball (h • (y : X)) ε := by
    rw [Metric.smul_ball, proj_glue, hgy]
  have hsub (w : X) (hw : w ∈ ball (proj hP (glue hP a y)) ε) : g⁻¹ • w ∈ W :=
    hball (hmaps ▸ smul_mem_smul_set hw)
  refine ⟨fun w ↦ chartLift hP M g (glue hP a y) (g⁻¹ • w),
    (continuousOn_chartLift hP hc g _).comp (continuous_const_smul _).continuousOn hsub, ?_,
    fun w hw ↦ by simp only [proj_chartLift hP hc g _ (hsub w hw), smul_inv_smul], ?_⟩
  · rw [← image_image (chartLift hP M g (glue hP a y)) (g⁻¹ • ·), image_smul, hmaps]
    exact isOpen_image_chartLift hP hc g _ isOpen_ball hball
  · simp only [proj_glue, hgy]
    rw [chartLift_smul hP hc g _ hh y.2 (hball (mem_ball_self hε)), inv_mul_cancel_right]

end Gluing

/-! ### The global tessellation -/

variable [IsIsometricSMul G X]

/-- **Coincidences of translates are local.** For a local tiling with uniform charts of a simply
connected, locally connected metric space, an element `γ` of the group generated by the local
neighbours which carries a point `x ∈ P` to a point of `P` is a local neighbour at `γ • x`. -/
theorem IsLocalTiling.mem_of_smul_mem [LocallyConnectedSpace X] [SimplyConnectedSpace X]
    (hP : IsLocalTiling P N)
    (hu : HasUniformTilingCharts P N) {γ : G} (hγ : γ ∈ Subgroup.closure (⋃ x ∈ P, N x))
    {x : X} (hx : x ∈ P) (hγx : γ • x ∈ P) : γ ∈ N (γ • x) := by
  have h := IsCoveringMap.eq_of_joined (isCoveringMap_proj hP hu)
    (joined_glue hP hγ ⟨γ • x, hγx⟩ ⟨x, hx⟩)
    (by rw [proj_glue, proj_glue, one_smul])
  simpa using ((glue_eq_glue_iff hP).1 h).2

/-- **The translates of the tile are locally finite.** For a local tiling with uniform charts of
a simply connected, locally connected metric space, the translates of `P` by the group generated
by the local neighbours form a locally finite family. -/
theorem IsLocalTiling.locallyFinite_smul [LocallyConnectedSpace X] [SimplyConnectedSpace X]
    (hP : IsLocalTiling P N) (hu : HasUniformTilingCharts P N) :
    LocallyFinite fun γ : Subgroup.closure (⋃ x ∈ P, N x) ↦ (γ : G) • P := by
  -- near `γ₀ • y` with `y ∈ P`, every translate meeting the translated chart of `y` is
  -- `γ₀ • h • P` for a local neighbour `h` of `y`, and the chart of `y` is locally finite
  set Γ := Subgroup.closure (⋃ x ∈ P, N x)
  intro z
  obtain ⟨γ₀, hγ₀, hzγ₀⟩ := mem_iUnion₂.1 (hP.iUnion_smul_eq_univ hu ▸ mem_univ z)
  obtain ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩ := mem_smul_set.1 hzγ₀
  obtain ⟨W, hyW, hc⟩ := hP.exists_isTilingChart y hy
  obtain ⟨t, ht, hfin⟩ := hc.locallyFinite y
  refine ⟨γ₀ • (W ∩ t),
    (smul_mem_nhds_smul_iff γ₀).2 (Filter.inter_mem (hc.isOpen.mem_nhds hyW) ht),
    ((hfin.image fun h : N y ↦ γ₀ * h).preimage Subtype.val_injective.injOn).subset ?_⟩
  rintro ⟨γ, hγ⟩ ⟨w, hwγ, hwW⟩
  dsimp only at hwγ hwW
  obtain ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩ := mem_smul_set.1 hwγ
  obtain ⟨hu', hut⟩ := mem_smul_set_iff_inv_smul_mem.1 hwW
  obtain ⟨h, hh, huh⟩ := mem_iUnion₂.1 (hc.subset_iUnion_smul hu')
  have hv := mem_smul_set_iff_inv_smul_mem.1 huh
  -- `(γ₀ * h)⁻¹ * γ` carries `x` into `P`, so it is a local neighbour there
  have hkx : ((γ₀ * h)⁻¹ * γ) • x = h⁻¹ • γ₀⁻¹ • γ • x := by
    rw [mul_inv_rev, mul_smul, mul_smul]
  have hk : (γ₀ * h)⁻¹ * γ ∈ N (((γ₀ * h)⁻¹ * γ) • x) := hP.mem_of_smul_mem hu
    (Γ.mul_mem (Γ.inv_mem (Γ.mul_mem hγ₀ (Subgroup.subset_closure (mem_iUnion₂.2 ⟨y, hy, hh⟩))))
      hγ) hx (hkx ▸ hv)
  rw [hkx] at hk
  have hγ₀γ : γ₀⁻¹ * γ ∈ N y := by
    simpa [mul_assoc] using hc.mul_mem h hh _ hv (by rwa [smul_inv_smul]) _ hk
  -- so `γ = γ₀ * (γ₀⁻¹ * γ)` with `γ₀⁻¹ * γ` a tile of the chart through `γ₀⁻¹ • γ • x`
  refine ⟨⟨γ₀⁻¹ * γ, hγ₀γ⟩, ⟨γ₀⁻¹ • γ • x, ⟨?_, hu'⟩, hut⟩, by simp⟩
  rw [mul_smul]
  exact smul_mem_smul_set (smul_mem_smul_set hx)

end TauCeti
